<h1 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 10px;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Historical Sites and Tourism – Lesson # 4</h1>
<p style="text-align: center; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 20px;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 33%;"><b>Grade:</b> 9th Grade (CEFR: A2.4)</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 33%;"><b>Scenario:</b> Historical Sites and Tourism</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 34%;"><b>Theme:</b> Take a Trip to the Panama Canal</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 50%;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 50%;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td colspan="3" style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Write simple texts giving key information about oneself and one's culture. Interactive: Edit narrative texts written by peers.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write a simple text sharing a personal cultural tradition (e.g., "Describe your family's celebration of Carnival and explain a key tradition, such as attending parades or dancing at the culcos."). Can edit a peer's narrative on Indigenous traditions by suggesting additional details (e.g., "I think you can add more details about the colors in traditional clothing."). Can edit a peer's descriptive paragraph on a festival (e.g., "You could add some adjectives like 'colorful' or 'exciting' to make it sound more vivid and fun.")."</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 30px; margin-bottom: 15px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 34%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a large picture of the Panama Canal (e.g., Miraflores Locks, ships transiting). Students are asked to write down three adjectives or short phrases that describe what they see or feel when looking at the image. They share their words with a partner, then a few share with the class. This activates vocabulary related to "historical," "famous," "important," "big," "cultural," "informative."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher writes two simple descriptive sentences on the board about a famous landmark (e.g., "The Golden Gate Bridge is a very **famous monument** in San Francisco. It **attracts** many **visitors** every year."). The teacher highlights the use of adjectives and verbs, emphasizing pronunciation for "famous" and "attracts" and focusing on stress in "monument" and "visitors." The teacher explains that today's focus is on writing clear, descriptive sentences about historical sites.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Are we going to speak or write today?" (Expected answer: Write.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I say 'descriptive sentences,' what kind of words should you use?" (Expected answer: Adjectives, words that tell us about something.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Historical Sites and Tourism")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short informative paragraph (about 60-80 words) from a tourist brochure or website describing the historical significance of the Panama Canal and what a visitor typically experiences there. The text incorporates grammar (Present Simple, Simple Past, possessive 's) and target vocabulary (Panama Canal, historical sites, landmarks, destination, attract, visit, transit, learn).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Example Text:</b> "The Panama Canal is one of the world's most **famous historical sites** and an incredible **landmark**. It **attracts** thousands of **visitors** every year. This amazing waterway **was built** to connect the Atlantic and Pacific oceans, and it **changed** global trade. Today, people **visit** the Miraflores Locks to **learn** about its **heritage** and watch gigantic ships **transit**. Many **are going to explore** the museum and enjoy the **informative** exhibits about **Panama's** engineering marvel."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Understanding intent and context. "The tone of this article is informative because it provides detailed historical facts about Casco Viejo." (Adapted for Panama Canal)</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks (Written):</b> Students read the text silently, then write short answers to these questions:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What is the main purpose of the Panama Canal?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What can visitors do at Miraflores Locks?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What tense is used to describe how the Canal changed global trade?</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Writing)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Writing sentences and short paragraphs using Present Simple, Simple Past for describing places and importance, Future tense with "going to" for plans, Possessive forms with 's. Target vocabulary: historical sites, Panama Canal, landmarks, architecture, heritage, monument, destination, visitor, museum, attract, visit, explore, preserve, describe, informative, renowned.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice (Fill-in-the-blanks & Tense Choice):</b> Students complete sentences in writing. The teacher provides sentences with blanks and choices for verbs in different tenses or target vocabulary.
                        <br>Example: "The Panama Canal ___ (is / was) a **renowned** engineering feat. Many tourists ___ (attracts / attract) its locks daily. My family and I ___ (going to visit / are going to visit) it next summer."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice (Sentence Expansion & Rewriting):</b> Students are given simple sentences and asked to rewrite them, adding descriptive adjectives and using specific grammar points.
                        <br>Example: "Panama Canal is big." -> Rewrite, adding adjectives and mentioning its importance. (Expected: "The Panama Canal is an incredibly **important** and **famous historical site**.")
                        <br>Example: "The Canal connects oceans." -> Rewrite, using possessive 's and future plans. (Expected: "The Canal connects the oceans. **Panama's** government **is going to preserve** its **heritage**.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Collaborative Sentence Writing (Peer Check):</b> In pairs, students receive three prompts related to the Panama Canal (e.g., "Describe its history," "Mention what visitors do," "Talk about future plans"). Each student writes one sentence per prompt, then they exchange and check each other's sentences for correct grammar (tenses, possessive 's) and appropriate vocabulary, making suggestions for improvements in writing.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-18 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Historical Sites and Tourism")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Individual descriptive paragraph writing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Task:</b> Students will individually write a short descriptive paragraph (5-7 sentences) for a tourist website about the Panama Canal. The paragraph should:
                    <ul style="list-style-type: circle; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Introduce the Panama Canal as a key historical site and landmark.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Describe its importance or a key historical fact using the Simple Past.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Mention what visitors can see or do there now, using the Present Simple.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Include a plan for a future visit or activity related to the Canal, using "going to."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Incorporate at least four different target vocabulary words (e.g., historical sites, monument, destination, attract, explore, informative, heritage).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use at least one possessive form ('s).</li>
                    </ul>
                    Students are encouraged to use adjectives to make their writing more vivid and fun (e.g., "colorful," "exciting," "vibrant").
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Peer Assessment using a checklist.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students exchange their written paragraphs from Stage 4 with a peer. Each student receives a "Peer Editing Checklist" and uses it to evaluate their partner's writing. They provide constructive feedback in writing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (on checklist):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Does the paragraph include at least 4 target vocabulary words (e.g., **landmarks**, **heritage**, **destination**, **attracts**)? (Yes/No)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Are Present Simple and Simple Past tenses used correctly? (Yes/Needs improvement)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Is "going to" used correctly for a future plan? (Yes/Needs improvement)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Is at least one possessive form ('s) used correctly? (Yes/No)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Is the text clear and easy to understand? (Yes/No)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(Peer Suggestion): "You could add some adjectives like 'colorful' or 'exciting' to make it sound more vivid and fun here: ______."</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer the following questions on a small slip of paper before leaving:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What was one new word or grammar point you used effectively in your writing today?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What was one suggestion your peer gave you that you will use to improve your writing?</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">How confident do you feel now about writing a short description of a historical site?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What was the most challenging part of writing and editing today, and why?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> Most students were able to correctly apply the Present Simple and some target vocabulary in their descriptions. The use of Simple Past for historical facts and "going to" for future plans showed varying degrees of accuracy; some students confused tenses. The peer editing was effective in highlighting common errors and encouraging interactive feedback. Pronunciation of multisyllabic words like "historical" and "information" was implicitly reinforced as students read their peers' work silently. Next time, I need to provide more scaffolded examples for combining tenses within a single descriptive sentence. I could also focus on comparing and contrasting historical details in writing, encouraging students to explain *why* something is important, linking to the pragmatic competence.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> This writing lesson on describing historical sites and editing peers' work will prepare students for the final mediation and integration lesson (Lesson 5), where they will consolidate information about the Panama Canal and other historical sites to create a persuasive presentation or a short informative guide, likely requiring them to summarize and synthesize their written ideas into an oral or multimedia product. The ability to write clear descriptions and edit effectively will be crucial for the quality of their final project.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">3-5 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>